🟠 logstore in observability (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim chunks is out of space. It fails with "level=error msg="flush chunks" err="write /var/lib/logstore/chunks/1f3a: no space left on device"". The error mentions it. Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago. Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/chunks → spec.resources.requests.storage (50Gi). To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run kubectl describe pvc chunks -n observability
🟠 logstore in observability (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim chunks is out of space.
| 🟠 **logstore** in **observability** (**prod-eu-1**) keeps crashing because volume claim **chunks** is out of space.
| It fails with
| ```
| level=error msg="flush chunks" err="write /var/lib/logstore/chunks/1f3a: no space left on device"
| ```
| The error mentions it.
| Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago.
| Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/chunks → spec.resources.requests.storage (50Gi).
| To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run
| ```
